// test-error
// test-adr: 016
// Issue #1333: reopening COMPOSES a scope; it does not relax member uniqueness.
//
// This is the negative control for the reopening fix. An assertion catches
// under-enforcement (a scope that cannot be reopened); this catches
// OVER-enforcement -- a fix that stopped reporting genuine duplicate members
// because they happened to be written in different blocks.
//
// Members are grouped by the scope's own identity, not by the declaration block,
// so these two definitions of Lib.useIt collide exactly as they would inside one
// block.
//
// The assertion in .expected.error is DELIBERATELY GENERIC and is weaker than this
// fixture's intent. It pins only the wrapper message:
//
//     1:0 Symbol conflicts detected - cannot proceed
//
// which names no symbol, so any symbol conflict satisfies it. The specific line --
// "Symbol conflict: 'Lib.useIt' is defined multiple times in C-Next" -- carries no
// usable position: the conflict is reported at 1:0 rather than at the offending
// declaration. That is #1334, and it is the same defect that stops ADR-016's matrix
// cells from being occupiable. Strengthening this assertion is blocked on it.

scope Lib {
    public u32 useIt() {
        return 1;
    }
}

scope Lib {
    public u32 useIt() {
        return 2;
    }
}

u32 main() {
    return Lib.useIt();
}
